"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI was drawn to the book by its title.  \n was already known to me through the book White Light.  \nActually, White Light wasn't 'very interesting' so I read this without much expectation for the author.  \n\n - this one sentence explains this book.  \nIt was a trick-finding book to discover why the title is 7 People 1 Role instead of 1 Person 7 Roles.  \n\nIt was an interesting and fun book that reads smoothly as the confessions and delusions from each suspect's perspective give readers more and more confusion.  \nI should read Renjo Mikihiko's other works as well."